WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.680
Hope is not a strategy.

2
00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:02.720
This is one of those areas where

3
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.260
I think we can be guilty of

4
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.400
being too optimistic.

5
00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:07.170
We have a conversation with a customer

6
00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.610
and somewhere along the way they mentioned

7
00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.610
they might be looking at buying another

8
00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.390
machine, expanding your fleet,

9
00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.150
or taking on a new project.

10
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.090
So what happens?

11
00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.230
We put it in our pipeline.

12
00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.390
Six months later it's still sitting there.

13
00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:20.850
Maybe we've talked to the customer once

14
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.690
or twice but nothing's really changed.

15
00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.830
So here's the question.

16
00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.210
Is that actually an opportunity or is

17
00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.030
that something we're hoping will eventually turn

18
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:30.215
into an opportunity?

19
00:00:30.215 --> 00:00:31.540
Because there's a big difference.

20
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:32.540
And I think that's where a lot

21
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:34.340
of pipelines get inflated.

22
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.020
We started adding up everything we've ever

23
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.300
talked to a customer about and suddenly

24
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.900
we have $5 million worth of pipeline.

25
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:42.720
Looks great on paper,

26
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.040
but how much of that business do

27
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.220
we realistically expect to close?

28
00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.900
I'd rather have a salesperson show me

29
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.740
a realistic $2 million pipeline than an

30
00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.520
inflated $5 million pipeline they can't explain.

31
00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.040
We're not trying to make our pipeline

32
00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:55.740
look impressive.

33
00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.260
We're trying to make it accurate.
